    <!-- Aisle floor. The old pale beige (0.55/0.68) sat right on top of the
         glass walls' pale blue (0.62/0.68): from the Gazebo camera the floor
         and the walls were the same colour and you could not see where an
         aisle ran. Dark slate-green reads clearly against both the walls and
         the brown ground, and stays well clear of the harvester's excess-red
         test (green suppresses r-g, so it can never be taken for fruit).

         Six strips now, not two: the four aisles plus the two end lanes.
         Together they ARE the survey circuit driven during the mapping laps,
         so the route is painted on the floor. Aisles are centred on
         y = -1.85 / -0.60 / +0.60 / +1.85, which are the free bands left
         between the walls (inner faces y = +/-2.45) and the three 0.4 m
         gutters at y = -1.2 / 0.0 / +1.2. -->
    <model name="aisle_pos">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 0.6 0.001 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <visual name="v">
          <geometry><box><size>9.70 0.72 0.002</size></box></geometry>
